          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.16,
            0.553,
            0.18
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Write formulas for the perimeter of:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.184,
            0.537,
            0.204
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) triangle with all sides equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.209,
            0.848,
            0.265
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) a regular pentagon (as we have learnt last year, we use the word ‘regular’ to say that all sidelengths and angle measures are equal)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.269,
            0.44,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(c) a regular hexagon"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.294,
            0.848,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Munirathna has a 20 m long pipe. However, he wants a longer watering pipe for his garden. He joins another pipe of some length to this one. Give the expression for the combined length of the pipe. Use the letter-number ‘k’ to denote the length in meters of the other pipe."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.372,
            0.848,
            0.412
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. What is the total amount Krithika has, if she has the following numbers of notes of ₹100, ₹20 and ₹5? Complete the following table:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.416,
            0.823,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.173,
                0.416,
                0.823,
                0.663
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_table_9.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tr><td>No. of₹100 notes</td><td>No. of₹20 notes</td><td>No. of₹5 notes</td><td>Expression and totalamount</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>5</td><td>6</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td><eq>\\begin{array}{c}6 \\times 100 + 4 \\times 20 + 3 \\times 5 \\\\= 695\\end{array}</eq></td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>4</td><td>Z</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>X</td><td>y</td><td>Z</td><td></td></tr></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.679,
            0.848,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Venkatalakshmi owns a flour mill. It takes 10 seconds for the roller mill to start running. Once it is running, each kg of grain takes 8 seconds to grind into powder. Which of the expressions below describes the time taken to complete grind ‘y’ kg of grain, assuming the machine is off initially?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.776,
            0.677,
            0.798
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 + 8 + y"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (b) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 1 0 \\pm 8 ) \\times y"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.801,
            0.665,
            0.822
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 \\times 8 \\times y"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (d) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 + 8 \\times y"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.825,
            0.352,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(e) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 \\times y + 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.849,
            0.745,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Write algebraic expressions using letters of your choice."
